  "source_findings": [
    "GlobalConfigContext was16 bytes on x86: domain pointer0, publication reference4, strings8, effectsCh. It is now20 bytes: SoundLifetimeAccess pointers0/4, publication8, stringsCh, effects10h. Owner storage remains2E8h.",
    "Current getter symbol#76 atCOFF fileCD1h uses context+8 atoffset30h, passes the two-word access value to captured guard at45h, publishes at175h, calls second manager getter17Dh before reloading slot182h/188h, registers18Bh, destroys guard193h, then final reload198h/19Bh. Plain RET1B7h.",
    "The old/current destructor primary spans are both429 bytes and differ at exactly four operand displacements: effectsCh->10h; strings8->Ch atEA/155h; publication4->8 at197h. Names and cdecl stack arity are unchanged.",
    "The unchanged lifetime adapter object hash6c1c57ee2dca156e51b2493d051e4603bff5a5b117de7fe2c9732b6f7124a375 stores a captured raw section atguard+4, enters it, increments+18h, then decrements and leaves that same pointer. Its semantic branch keeps the previous provider operations.",
    "CapturedSoundLifetimeSection constructor is compiled thiscall: ECX=this, two-word SoundLifetimeAccess by value on stack, EAX=this, RET8. Its destructor usesECX and plain RET. SoundLifetimeAccess getter usesECX plus hidden stack return-buffer pointer, writes the8-byte view, returns that pointer inEAX and RET4.",
    "SoundServices constructor current symbol#6438 relocates atfunction+2A5h through symbol#6177 toGameVfsHost::borrow_raw_services. It reads view+18h at2AFh, stores that referenced storage atlocal-A4h, and copies it into GameSoundRuntimeServices+1Ch at363h. No storage wrapper is copied or constructed by that view.",
    "GameSoundRuntime startup remains thiscall(ECX=this, stack disabled), RET4. At84h it pushes Impl+24h (services.strings), calls new startup through symbol#2573 atD8h, and cleans34h atDDh. Source services remains the first Impl field after its vtable bases.",
    "Startup reads the thirteenth argument atEBP+38h, retains it atlocal-30h, and passes it to both resource construction and Lua configuration. Initializer passesEBP+1Ch to the fragment before its18h cleanup; Lua open/load/apply/close order is unchanged.",
    "NativeName constructor symbol#1221 stores its supplied storage atthis+0 and initializes theNativeString atthis+4; RET8. Destructor symbol#1222 pushes savedthis+0 and calls release_to onthis+4. The inlined listener/group lambda#1262 captures the same storage and releases group then listener with their saved values at204h/20Fh. Old CRT-getter edges at those sites are replaced.",
    "Category lambda#1251 pushes its captured storage before create_sound_class at2Fh. SoundClassDescriptor stores its storage pointer and destroys its name through that pointer; construction/destruction therefore use one wrapper.",
    "Application source order constructs VFS/Lua/scripts beforeSoundServices, binds the runtime beforestartup, drains raw singletons whileSound/Lua/VFS remain alive, resetsSound before deleting singletons, and deletesVFS afterLua teardown. Existing exception recovery uses the same retained shutdown/storage services. This is static ownership/control-flow evidence, not a runtime-lifetime test.",
    "GameNativeVfsRawServices.strings is a reference member to the NativeVfsOwnerServices wrapper owned by the VFS application. The returned by-value view does not own or shorten that wrapper lifetime. Matching underlying process cells would not make another wrapper identical.",
    "Public trailing defaults preserve old-arity Source calls after recompilation. They do not preserve old function-pointer types, old Sound decorated names, or old context layout. No old-symbol overload/thunk is introduced. Current source census has exactly one runtime->startup, one startup->initializer, and one initializer->fragment call, all explicit storage forwarding.",
    "GlobalConfig getter/destructor/scalar-delete and constructor have no entries in the final bsp_game map; their current COFF exists but this audit does not claim game linkage/execution for them. The new Sound startup/initializer/fragment each has a positive final map provider entry."
  ],
